<title>VIRGIN ISLANDS: Virgin Islands Water &amp; Power seeks bond increase.</title>
<headline>Virgin Islands Water &amp; Power seeks bond increase.</headline>
<dateline>ST. THOMAS, U.S. Virgin Islands 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Virgin Islands Water &amp; Power Authority will ask the U.S. territory's legislature to raise its bond ceiling by $90 million, to $220 million, the agency's chief financial officer said Monday.</p>
<p>Utility CFO Terry Drake informed the Public Service Commission of the plan on Friday. He said the current $130 million bond ceiling was inadequate to fund pending projects at the utility, which already has $127 million of revenue bonds outstanding.</p>
<p>Drake proposed issuing $90 million of five-year revenue bonds to relocate the utility's business office, improve production plants and fund hazard mitigation projects. He said the debt would not require a rate increase for two years.</p>
<p>--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013</p>
